From 191b00d33cbfa4c690551d15013f0aee3de79fc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:44:24 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 42/60] Muse Spark: route on the fp32 normed MoE input, per-row
 key chunks, a one-GPU TP pair

Router: muse_gate_norm also writes the normed MoE input unrounded (xf) and muse_router reads it, as exllamav3's
muse_spark patch 0004 does (the fp16-rounded input flipped near-tied top-8 choices); the experts still read the
fp16 cast.

Attention: a full layer's chunk width is a function of the row's own position (256 keys up to a 16K bucket, then
bucket / 64 rounded to 256), computed in muse_attn_rows, so a row gets the same bits in any window at any context
and no window needs more than 64 chunks (the partial buffers stay small at 128K context).

pair.zig: a test-only tp.Collective joining two host threads on one GPU (device copies at a spin barrier);
tf-muse m1 MUSE_PAIR=1 runs both ranks of TP=2 in one process (eager only), for checking the two-rank arithmetic
beside a conversion that holds the other node. NCCL refuses two ranks on one device.
